  "finalText": "Config is valid and install succeeds. Here's the summary:\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem:** Your `.npmrc` contained three non-auth settings (`shamefully-hoist`, `strict-peer-dependencies`, `lockfile`) that pnpm 10+ silently ignores. The `shamefully-hoist=true` setting would silently revert to `false` (strict isolation), potentially breaking workspace scripts that rely on phantom dependencies.\n\n**Fix applied:**\n1. Migrated all three settings to `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (which pnpm 10+ reads for all non-auth settings)\n2. Cleared `.npmrc` of non-auth content (retained for future auth settings)\n\n**No breakage from `--resolution-only`:** Not used in this repo.\n\n**Note on `packageManager` field:** The repo still pins `pnpm@9.15.0`. The config migration makes the settings forward-compatible with pnpm 10/11/12, but you'll eventually want to bump `packageManager` in `package.json` and run `pnpm install` to regenerate the lockfile in the new format.\n\n**Sources checked:**\n- https://pnpm.io/12.x/settings — \"Only auth and registry settings are read from `.npmrc` files\"\n- https://pnpm.io/12.x/settings/node-modules#shamefullyhoist\n- https://pnpm.io/12.x/settings/peer-dependencies#strictpeerdependencies\n- https://pnpm.io/12.x/settings/store#lockfile\n- https://pnpm.io/blog/whats-different-in-pnpm-12 — `--resolution-only` removal\n- https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/releases — latest v12.3.4",
